% Exercise: integer division
%
% Prolog has two division operators. The one for integer floor-division
% is `//`:
%
%     X is 10 // 3.    % X = 3   (3.33... rounded down)
%     Y is 100 // 25.  % Y = 4
%     Z is 7 // 2.     % Z = 3
%
% The companion operator `mod` gives the remainder:
%
%     R is 10 mod 3.   % R = 1
%     R is 100 mod 7.  % R = 2
%
% Your task: define a rule `answer(X)` that uses `//` to compute how
% many full dozens are in 100 (i.e. 100 // 12).
